<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramgarhia misl</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ramgarhia misl was one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-confederacy">Sikh confederacies</a> of 18th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, named after the fort of Ramgarh at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amritsar">Amritsar</a> and led by Jassa Singh Ramgarhia. It held territory around Batala and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bist-doab">Jalandhar Doab</a> and was a rival of the Ahluwalia and Kanhaiya misls. Its lands were absorbed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a> in the early 19th century.</p></div>
